{title: His Praise Will Always Be On My Lips}
{subtitle: Psalms 34:1–3}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Cm7] |
| [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Of David when he feigned [Abmaj7]madness
Before Abimelech who [Cm7]drove him away
He left and found [Abmaj7]his true rest
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm7]I will bless the LORD [Abmaj7]at all times
His [Eb]praise will always be [Bb]on my lips
[Cm7]My soul boasts in the [Abmaj7]LORD
Let the [Eb]humble hear and re[Bb]joice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Magnify the LORD [Abmaj7]with me
[Cm7]Let us exalt [Bb]his name together
[Eb]I sought the LORD and he [Abmaj7]answered me
He de[Cm7]livered me [Bb]from all my [Eb]fears
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Cm7] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Those who look to him are [Abmaj7]radiant
Their faces will [Cm7]never be ashamed
I will bless the LORD at [Abmaj7]all times
His [Cm7]praise will always be [Abmaj7]on my lips
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Cm7] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]His praise will always [Abmaj7]be on my lips
[Cm7]Magnify the [Bb]LORD with [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}
